    {
      "title": "Modi and Vijay commit themselves to working together for Tamil Nadu’s development",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/modi-and-vijay-commit-themselves-to-working-together-for-tamil-nadus-development/article71571973.ece",
      "description": "Inaugurating a slew of projects, including the Chennai Metro Rail services on the Vadapalani-Poonamallee stretch, Mr. Modi says that while governments have changed, his commitment to the development of Tamil Nadu and his service to its people have remained the same",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-11T15:42:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Will work with CM Vijay for TN's growth, development my 'mantra', says PM",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/will-work-with-cm-vijay-for-tn-s-growth-development-my-mantra-says-pm-126101100389_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Sunday said he has taken development as his 'mantra,' and reaffirmed his commitment to serve the people of Tamil Nadu and ensuring the state's progress by working with Chief Minister C Joseph Vijay.\nHe listed out the rapid strides made in various sectors in the last 12 years, including the significant jump in defence exports.\nIn his address after inaugurating and laying the foundation stone for railway, road and petroleum-related projects worth about Rs 13,000 crore with Vijay, the PM underscored his commitment to ensure development.\n\"I have always taken country's development as my mantra,\" he said.\n\"As chief minister, I understood the expectations of a state. After becoming PM, not only did I try to fulfil the aspirations but also made efforts so that the states meet their aspiration goals,\" he said.\nReferring to Tamil Nadu, he said when he was CM,  he got the opportunity to interact with late leaders M Karunanidhi and J Jayalalithaa when they head",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-11T11:02:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "PM Modi inaugurates projects worth over ₹13,000 crore in Tamil Nadu",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/pm-modi-inaugurates-projects-worth-over-13-000-crore-in-tamil-nadu-126101100328_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Sunday inaugurated and laid the foundation stones for various development projects worth over Rs 13,000 crore across Tamil Nadu.\nThe initiatives included those in the road and rail transport and petroleum sectors.\nThe PM, along with Tamil Nadu Chief Minister C Joseph Vijay, inaugurated and laid the foundation stones for the developments projects at an event held at the IIT, Madras.\nThe projects include those in National Highways worth around Rs 3,700 crore, initiatives in the Chennai Port, Kamarajar Port and V O Chidambaranar Port and Amrit railway stations. He also dedicated to the nation, the Sudha Gopalakrishnan Brain Centre (SGBC) at IIT Madras.\nSGBC is a pioneering global scientific mission to map more than 100 human brains into three-dimensional atlases at cellular resolution, across the human lifespan - from the foetal stage to old age.\nThe PM also released C-STROKE, a one-of-a-kind human ischaemic stroke atlas. Featuring over 1,000 annotated",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-11T10:15:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "PM Modi holds roadshow in Chennai, to launch projects worth ₹13,000 crore",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/pm-modi-holds-roadshow-in-chennai-to-launch-projects-worth-13-000-crore-126101100173_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi arrived here on Sunday to lay the foundation stone for projects and also dedicate projects worth over Rs 13,000 crore.\nUpon his arrival at the airport by 11 am, Chief Minister C Joseph Vijay accorded him a warm welcome.\nPM Modi briefly held a roadshow and waved at the BJP workers and supporters who lined up behind barricades near the airport to welcome him.\nAs Modi's motorcade moved out of the airport, a serpentine queue of BJP workers and supporters waiting on roadsides waved to him and raised \"Bharat Mata Ki Jai,\" slogans.\nTamil Nadu BJP accorded him a warm welcome by also holding cultural programmes like traditional dance shows on specially earmarked spaces on the roadside near the airport.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-11T06:56:06"
    }
  ]
}